  "note": "Election of the Dungannon Urban Council, ordinary day 15 January 1932; there were no contests and the new Council, fourteen Unionists and seven Nationalists, was returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 6 January 1932, p. 9). Returned unopposed. All seven names confirmed on the block image of the cited article (BNL19320106.2.179), which prints 'M. T. Roberts'; the OCR reads Beattie as Beittie. Returned unopposed."
